From 2855c7e7eb86c3b6abd2209db611677bdc3f0929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:44:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bend2: an asynchronous scheduler for waits that no file
 descriptor backs

A parked effect with no fd and at = Infinity is an external wait: its event (a WebSocket
message, a host timer) calls io_notify, and the next io_wait calls its more() to see whether it
is done. The top-level run now awaits io_wait_async, which blocks in neither select nor a
busy loop, so the host's event loop keeps running while a program waits on it. Waits on fds
keep the blocking poll.

The run loop is a generator (io_steps) driven two ways: io_run_async for the program's own run
(and the exit of a compiled program), and io_run, the blocking poll, for a nested run started
from an effect, which cannot await. The compiler's entry point and book_run await the result.

Checked: the 234 I/O tests of tests/io give the same output and exit codes as before, apart
from the checkout's path in three tests that name it, and a fork_join ordering that flipped
under eight parallel jobs (it matches its expected order when run alone). A program waiting
on a host timer and a program that awaits a WebSocket relay (browser/runtime in the project)
both complete, and a compiled program runs.

